From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:21:09 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] Plutonium: remote clients see native windows

Away from the desktop (another machine's browser) the Apps panel has no
<native-window>. The server streams windows instead, through the helper's
socket: /api/window-stream/ws sends the window list, and with ?windowId the
window's JPEG frames; the client sends mouse and key input back
(preview:operate). The web app fills the window store from that list outside
the shell and draws a window's tab on a canvas (RemoteWindowView).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
